{"id": "section-body-16421", "title": "Laryngitis", "chapterId": "chapter-fifteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EAR, NOSE AND THROAT/HEAD AND NECK DISEASES", "Throat Conditions", "Laryngitis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-16421", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Laryngitis", "runs": [{"text": "Laryngitis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1219"}}, {"id": "body-16422", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Inflammatory condition of the larynx can be infectious or non-infectious, acute (3–7 days) or chronic (>3 weeks). Diagnosis is often made by case history alone and treatment often targets symptoms.", "runs": [{"text": "Inflammatory condition of the larynx can be infectious or non-infectious, acute (3–7 days) or chronic (>3 weeks). Diagnosis is often made by case history alone and treatment often targets symptoms."}]}, {"id": "body-16423", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Acute viral laryngitis is commonest and self-limiting, often linked to upper respiratory infections.", "runs": [{"text": "Acute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laryngitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "commonest"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "self-limiting,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "linked"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "upper"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infections."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1172"}}, {"id": "body-16424", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Bacterial laryngitis is less common but can be more severe.", "runs": [{"text": "Bacterial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laryngitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "less"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "common"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1172"}}, {"id": "body-16425", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Clinical Presentation may differ between children and adults.", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "differ"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "between"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "children"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "adults."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1172"}}, {"id": "body-16426", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Signs of infectious laryngitis include odynophagia, cough, fever, and respiratory distress.", "runs": [{"text": "Signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infectious"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laryngitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "odynophagia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cough,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "distress."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1172"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Ear, nose and throat/head and neck diseases", "start": "body-16421", "end": "body-16426"}}